    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'Why does model.execute return unauthorized_output when my host passes model evidence through?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'The Spec 104 host-private output filter in the native executor rejects any connector output string that starts with / or contains ://. The full ModelRightsRecord that Spec 138 hosts return carries source_url values (https:// URLs), so forwarding it verbatim from a connector bridge into the catalog model.execute@1.0.0 guest fails with unauthorized_output (-4). Bridges currently have to pick fields by hand. registry#641 tracks defining a normative model_evidence shape so every host emits the same bytes; it is open.',
